{"id":"7cd699c85c4618c0","group":"67","path":"67/67-thm-pi-conservativity-disjunction.md","title":"Pi Conservativity Detects a Provable Disjunction","display":"thm-pi-conservativity-disjunction — Pi Conservativity Detects a Provable Disjunction","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom","book_abbrev":"67","label":"67-thm-pi-conservativity-disjunction","aliases":["67-thm-pi-conservativity-disjunction"],"display":"thm-pi-conservativity-disjunction — Pi Conservativity Detects a Provable Disjunction","depends_on":["[[67-lem-pi-conservative-splitting]]","[[67-df-partially-conservative]]","[[67-df-arithmetical-classes]]","[[67-df-PA]]","[[67-df-prim-provability]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf","source_edition":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition","source_chapter":5,"source_label":"observation before and after Lemma 5.5","source_printed_pages":[66],"source_pdf_pages":[77],"verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"source statement and printed argument checked; full auxiliary formalization not independently reconstructed","eligible_as_verified_dependency":false},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"67"},{"key":"label","html":"67-thm-pi-conservativity-disjunction"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>67-thm-pi-conservativity-disjunction</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-pi-conservativity-disjunction — Pi Conservativity Detects a Provable Disjunction"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d89be218ac107852\" href=\"?note=d89be218ac107852\" title=\"67-lem-pi-conservative-splitting\">67-lem-pi-conservative-splitting</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5d04e3c8a5885c18\" href=\"?note=5d04e3c8a5885c18\" title=\"67-df-partially-conservative\">67-df-partially-conservative</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"851cd80e64893935\" href=\"?note=851cd80e64893935\" title=\"67-df-arithmetical-classes\">67-df-arithmetical-classes</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"cd051851df5d2aa2\" href=\"?note=cd051851df5d2aa2\" title=\"67-df-PA\">67-df-PA</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"573b4c635ea6d91f\" href=\"?note=573b4c635ea6d91f\" title=\"67-df-prim-provability\">67-df-prim-provability</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition"},{"key":"source_chapter","html":"5"},{"key":"source_label","html":"observation before and after Lemma 5.5"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>66</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>77</span></div>"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"source statement and printed argument checked; full auxiliary formalization not independently reconstructed"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"false"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}\">\\(T\\supseteq\\mathrm{PA}\\)</span> 是一致的固定原始递归算术公理呈示，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\ge1\">\\(n\\ge1\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_n,\\Pi_n\">\\(\\Sigma_n,\\Pi_n\\)</span> 及相对公式类取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"851cd80e64893935\" href=\"?note=851cd80e64893935\" title=\"67-df-arithmetical-classes\">67-df-arithmetical-classes</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}\">\\(\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}\\)</span> 为算术句子集；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vdash\">\\(\\vdash\\)</span> 为 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"573b4c635ea6d91f\" href=\"?note=573b4c635ea6d91f\" title=\"67-df-prim-provability\">67-df-prim-provability</a> 的元语言有限可推导性。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\psi_0,\\psi_1\\in\\Pi_n\\cap\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}\">\\(\\psi_0,\\psi_1\\in\\Pi_n\\cap\\mathrm{Sent}_{L_A}\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Sigma_n}\">\\(\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Sigma_n}\\)</span> 取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"5d04e3c8a5885c18\" href=\"?note=5d04e3c8a5885c18\" title=\"67-df-partially-conservative\">67-df-partially-conservative</a>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\left(T\\vdash\\psi_0\\lor\\psi_1\\right)\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\bigwedge_{i&lt;2}\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Sigma_n}\\left(\\psi_i,T\\cup\\{\\neg\\psi_{1-i}\\}\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\left(T\\vdash\\psi_0\\lor\\psi_1\\right)\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\ \\bigwedge_{i&lt;2}\\mathrm{ConsSent}_{\\Sigma_n}\\left(\\psi_i,T\\cup\\{\\neg\\psi_{1-i}\\}\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>这是印刷66页/PDF77页引理5前后讨论的精确双向判准。顺向：已有 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\vdash\\psi_0\\lor\\psi_1\">\\(T\\vdash\\psi_0\\lor\\psi_1\\)</span> 时，添加另一侧否定即可证明当前句，所以扩张不增加任何后果。逆向：取引理5的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta_i\">\\(\\theta_i\\)</span>；在 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T+\\neg\\psi_i+\\psi_{1-i}\">\\(T+\\neg\\psi_i+\\psi_{1-i}\\)</span> 中，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta_i\">\\(\\theta_i\\)</span> 会与 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta_0\\land\\theta_1\\to\\psi_0\\land\\psi_1\">\\(\\theta_0\\land\\theta_1\\to\\psi_0\\land\\psi_1\\)</span> 矛盾，故证明 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\neg\\theta_i\">\\(\\neg\\theta_i\\)</span>。把它正规化成 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_n\">\\(\\Sigma_n\\)</span> 后，由保守性得到 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T+\\neg\\psi_i\\vdash\\neg\\theta_i\">\\(T+\\neg\\psi_i\\vdash\\neg\\theta_i\\)</span>，于是 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\vdash\\theta_i\\to\\psi_i\">\\(T\\vdash\\theta_i\\to\\psi_i\\)</span>。结合 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\vdash\\theta_0\\lor\\theta_1\">\\(T\\vdash\\theta_0\\lor\\theta_1\\)</span> 得到结论。前提允许 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T+\\neg\\psi_i\">\\(T+\\neg\\psi_i\\)</span> 不一致；这种情况下后果转移仍有意义，不额外假定两分支一致。</p>\n<p>此处有限逻辑推导已检查；结论的来源证明仍依赖引理5的层级正规化接口，继承其受限证明状态。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"67-lem-pi-conservative-splitting","status":"resolved","id":"d89be218ac107852","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-lem-pi-conservative-splitting]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-partially-conservative","status":"resolved","id":"5d04e3c8a5885c18","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-partially-conservative]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-arithmetical-classes","status":"resolved","id":"851cd80e64893935","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-arithmetical-classes]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-PA","status":"resolved","id":"cd051851df5d2aa2","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-PA]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-prim-provability","status":"resolved","id":"573b4c635ea6d91f","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"",